+  1. **Seed commitment**, before T_d0 of the first audited run: the founder generates the seed as 32 bytes from the operating system's cryptographic random source, written as 64 lowercase hex characters, and commits and pushes only SHA-256 of those 64 ASCII bytes (no newline). The seed is never disclosed to the harness author before step 3.
